<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Sept 30.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Sept 30.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    295.24   1.86</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	    272.66   3.79</p>
<p> 3   Mayne Nickless	 192.31   8.50</p>
<p> 4   Adel Bton Cement     123.19   1.70</p>
<p> 5   T N T		    117.27   1.63</p>
<p> 6   Colonial Coml	  116.94   2.14</p>
<p> 7   Herald Rsc	     100.88   1.14</p>
<p> 8   Forrestania Gold	83.33   2.10</p>
<p> 9   Westral Forest	  74.28   2.05</p>
<p>10   Cape Range		67.57   0.25</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	     2.90   0.70</p>
<p> 2   Computer Power	   3.22   3.30</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv		3.44   0.61</p>
<p> 4   Parbury Ltd		5.45   0.64</p>
<p> 5   BTR Plc		    6.23   5.80</p>
<p> 6   McIntosh Sec	     6.51   0.81</p>
<p> 7   Pac Mutal Aust	   6.58   2.35</p>
<p> 8   Aust Gold Rsc	    6.96   1.27</p>
<p> 9   OLS Asia Hldgs	   7.23   0.86</p>
<p>10   Capcount Prop	    7.59   0.83</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
